{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-09-26T16:43:46.361Z","author":"codex","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"d1738b58d58bd67fa4411935","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-jzp5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Hoisted broken pm-ops can bypass merge-driver install guard"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Greptile found that the canonical prepare launcher searches only the consumer checkout node_modules/pm-ops after a MODULE_NOT_FOUND resolution. Node also resolves packages from ancestor node_modules. If a hoisted pm-ops directory exists but lacks package.json, the launcher treats it as an omit-dev install and silently skips field-aware merge-driver registration. This extends the local broken-install guard in ops-eyi8 to the full Node lookup path."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":0},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-26T16:43:46.361Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-26T16:43:46.361Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A real child checkout with an empty ancestor node_modules/pm-ops fails the prepare hook without the omit-dev skip notice; a truly absent package still skips once; an intact hoisted pm-ops runs the installer; the regression fails on the old template, full release:check and strict PM health pass; consumer copies update only after a canonical pm-ops release."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf